id: pm-dm2vfz
title: Queued daily releases recognize an already-published same-day release before analyzer provenance
description: "A delayed scheduled Auto Release run queued behind a successful manual production release under workflow concurrency. When it began, main already pointed at the generated v2026.8.17 release commit. The workflow ran the reviewed-PR analyzer gate before any same-day release check, so the expected no-op path failed on direct-main release-commit provenance and opened GH-1045 even though GitHub, npm, npx, and bunx had already accepted the one immutable release for the UTC day. This is a distinct scheduling/concurrency recurrence: same-day uniqueness held, but the automatic path falsely reported a blocker after successful publication."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[6]: "area:release",ci,concurrency,github-actions,provenance,same-day-guard
created_at: "2026-08-17T03:40:44.831Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-17T04:40:25.710Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-17T04:12:29.398Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-17T04:12:29.398Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "A queued schedule or issue-retry run detects an already-published current-day tag before analyzer, dependency installation, version mutation, or release gates; The skip receipt identifies the authoritative existing tag and exact SHA and verifies GitHub Release plus npm publication rather than treating tag presence alone as success; A current-day tag whose publication is incomplete continues through immutable recovery or fails with a typed actionable blocker; it is never silently accepted; A schedule/manual concurrency negative control proves exactly one version is produced and the later automatic run completes successfully without a false blocker issue"
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: high
repro_steps: Dispatch a production Auto Release shortly before the delayed daily schedule becomes runnable; let the manual run push the current-day release commit/tag while the scheduled run waits on workflow concurrency; observe the scheduled checkout at the release commit fail reviewed-PR analyzer provenance before same-day skip logic.
resolution: "Automatic schedule and issue-retry events now resolve the current UTC-day immutable tag before analyzer or build work, select/wait/recover its exact Release workflow, and accept success only after direct non-draft GitHub Release plus anonymous exact-version npm verification. Manual workflow dispatch remains governed by the separate same-day follow-up policy."
expected_result: "After one production path publishes the UTC-day release, any queued automatic run recognizes and verifies that immutable result before analyzer provenance and exits successfully without a second release or blocker issue."
actual_result: "Behavioral workflow tests execute both tag detection and recovery shell paths: queued schedule returns the existing exact tag/SHA without issue mutation or republishing; missing public npm evidence fails closed. Focused PM-linked suite passes 35/35, full suite passes 7,459 tests at exact 100/100/100/100 coverage, security scan and production audit report zero findings, and package artifact validation passes."
affected_version: 2026.8.17
fixed_version: 2026.8.18
component: Auto Release workflow orchestration
